// ============================================================================
// Projections · SERVICE DESCRIPTORS  (META-INF/services)
//
// PROJECTIONS NEVER JOIN. These are named views over the two base relations so the
// resolution layer reads intent rather than column offsets; interpretation belongs in
// config-resolution/, not here.
//
// A provider-configuration file under META-INF/services names, in plain text, the classes
// that implement one service interface. The JVM instantiates each of them through
// ServiceLoader and calls the interface's methods on them, so a provider is BOTH an
// instantiation the analysis cannot otherwise see and an entry point.
//
// java_service_descriptor (14): 1 serviceInterface  4 packageName  6 isWellFormedServiceName
//                              14 serviceDescriptorUniqueHash
// java_service_provider   (19): 1 providerClass  3 simpleName  4 packageName
//                               7 isWellFormedName  15 serviceDescriptorLinkHash
//                              19 serviceProviderUniqueHash
// ============================================================================

// svc_descriptor(Descriptor, ServiceInterfaceName, WellFormed)
svc_descriptor(d, svc, wf) :- java_service_descriptor(svc, _, _, _, _, wf, _, _, _, _, _, _, _, d).

// svc_provider(Provider, Descriptor, PackageName, SimpleName)
// Only well-formed names: a malformed line is emitted by the parser WITH its columns left
// empty and flagged, precisely so a consumer cannot fabricate a class out of it.
svc_provider(p, d, pkg, simple) :- java_service_provider(_, _, simple, pkg, _, _, "true", _, _, _, _, _, _, _, d, _, _, _, p).
